     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This was discussed during the August 26 Fedora Tech Meeting (see ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "url": "https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FF/2021-08-26-+Fedora+Tech+Meeting"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": "  for full notes).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We agreed upon a minimum viable product that creates a thin route that uses the existing http service to POST messages to a configured API endpoint, with the option of basic authentication.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Some additional “nice to haves” include the ability to include configured arbitrary HTTP headers in the POST, the ability to filter which messages are passed along (perhaps using a simple substring match rule), and perhaps a JSON configuration file for managing these details (which in the future could be expanded to support messaging to multiple endpoints, etc., etc.).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
