  "customfield_10154": null,
  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It would be helpful to have a standard way to use the Camel Toolbox to facilitate messaging between Fedora and arbitrary third-party microservices/APIs.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For example: my use case is that whenever an object is added or modified in Fedora, I would like to POST the object's identifier to a web service that handles indexing. (My indexing process is quite complex and depends on other parts of my non-Java-based codebase, and so it makes more sense to handle it as an external microservice rather than trying to directly incorporate the whole indexing process into the Camel Toolbox).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It seems that it may be possible to create a configurable service in the toolbox which could meet my use case while also being flexible enough to support a significant number of other possible use cases. For example, if we could configure which types of actions trigger a message, the target URL, the HTTP method to use, and the payload (which could potentially be GET and/or POST parameters, or a message body).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I have full control over the nature of my own web service, so I can tailor the code I build to suit whatever implementation is easiest on the Camel Toolbox side – thus, I do not demand all this flexibility... but it might be helpful to others if easy to implement. I would be perfectly happy to start with a minimum viable product that is designed to be extensible in case of future need.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If others feel this is a good idea and would like to discuss a path forward, I am willing to lead an initial implementation, on the understanding that I'm unfamiliar with the platform and might need a little hand-holding to get things underway. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "id": "1f642",
        "shortName": ":slight_smile:",
        "text": "🙂"
       },
       "type": "emoji"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This topic was discussed on the August 12, 2021 Fedora Tech call.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
